          "semantic_invariants": [
            "A Grocery Round is a governed collective prepaid grocery-purchase programme over a defined plan period.",
            "Supported configured plan durations include 3, 6, 9 and 12 months.",
            "Members make scheduled prepaid grocery purchases or grocery credits during the plan period; the model is not a savings account or withdrawable cash pool.",
            "Member-level accounting preserves each member grocery entitlement and group transparency.",
            "Basket planning and equal member voting apply where the Round lifecycle requires collective decisions.",
            "After the relevant accumulation and planning stage, purchasing power is aggregated for bulk grocery procurement.",
            "Procured groceries are allocated against member entitlements and fulfilled as groceries; applicable Round benefits include free delivery."
          ],
          "semantic_guards": [
            "Grocery Rounds are not recurring grocery delivery or a Scheduled Basket.",
            "Grocery Rounds are not a flash group-buy, same-day neighbourhood wholesale order, savings account, investment pool or rotating cash mukando.",
            "Do not collapse Scheduled Basket into Grocery Rounds; they are separate customer products with different lifecycle semantics.",
            "Do not describe a Round as closing in hours merely to trigger an immediate group purchase unless authoritative Round state explicitly says so."
          ],
